<title>DUBAI: BP in Yemen lubricants joint venture.</title>
<headline>BP in Yemen lubricants joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Plc on Wednesday announced it had set up a joint venture lubricants venture in Yemen with the local Thabet Brothers Group.</p>
<p>The Yemeni-British Lubricants Marketing Company (SYC) would import lubricants from BP's blending plant at Jebel Ali in the United Arab Emirates for distribution throughout Yemen, a statement released in Dubai on behalf of BP said.</p>
<p>&quot;The lubricants imported will be premium quality and suitable for automotive, industrial and various commercial purposes,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Demand for lubricants and greases was growing an over 10 percent a year, it said.</p>
</text>
